{
  "baseline_version": "0.2",
  "note": "Pinned so that implementing a recognition predicate cannot move it. Recognition may convert a deferral into PASS or PARTIAL and nothing else: the UNKNOWN set, the FAIL set, the NOT_APPLICABLE set and the penalty total of every product must be unchanged by it. A diff here is not a test to update -- it is a recognition predicate that has introduced absence, a defect, or a penalty.",
  "repin": {
    "version": "0.2",
    "reason": "Re-pinned once, for P3.2 slice D, which is a *structural* semantics change carrying signed-off decision records -- not a recognition predicate, and not covered by the rule above. The movement is stated here exhaustively so the re-pin is reviewable rather than a silent rewrite of the thing that was supposed to be immovable.",
    "rubric_version": "0.3 -> 0.4",
    "decisions": [
      "D-029",
      "D-030",
      "D-031"
    ],
    "check_ids_whose_pinned_membership_moved": [
      "VARIANT.MEDIA_LINKED"
    ],
    "what_moved": "VARIANT.MEDIA_LINKED left the UNKNOWN set on the 11 products listed below and now defers there instead. Under D-031 the check runs only once a visual option name is found; on these products none is, so the previous UNKNOWN asserted a gap without having established that the check applied at all. Both states earn 0.00 and penalize 0.00, so no score moved -- what moved is that 11 `minor` findings are no longer emitted.",
    "products_where_media_linked_left_the_unknown_set": [
      "adv-02-category-implies-attributes::handle:trailpro-bike-helmet",
      "checks-04-non-inheritable::handle:checks-non-inheritable",
      "checks-06-duplicate-identifier::handle:checks-duplicate-sku",
      "checks-08-non-inheritable-recognition::handle:checks-scope-before-recognition",
      "rec-01-title-and-proportions::handle:rec-01-title-and-proportions",
      "rec-02-vague-phrases::handle:rec-02-vague-phrases",
      "rec-03-vague-in-a-sentence::handle:rec-03-vague-in-a-sentence",
      "rec-04-mixed-variant-coverage::handle:rec-04-mixed-variant-coverage",
      "rec-05-unreadable-variant-silences-the-check::handle:rec-05-unreadable-variant-silences-the-check",
      "sparse-apparel-02::handle:harbourline-everyday-tee",
      "sparse-sports-02::handle:tempo-training-mat"
    ],
    "what_did_not_move": "VARIANT.ATTRIBUTE_COVERAGE moved no pinned set on any existing product. Where it changed at all it went from a deferral to PARTIAL, which is the one transition the rule above already permits. No FAIL, no NOT_APPLICABLE and no penalty total changed anywhere in the corpus, and no other check_id moved in any set.",
    "products_added": [
      "rec-09-variant-scope-fully-covered::handle:rec-09-variant-scope-fully-covered",
      "rec-10-variant-scope-partly-covered::handle:rec-10-variant-scope-partly-covered",
      "rec-11-uncategorized-visual-option::handle:rec-11-uncategorized-visual-option"
    ]
  },
